  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support institutional capacities in drug control and prevention in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effectively addressing the challenges posed by drugs requires a balanced approach between drug enforcement and drug prevention. Therefore, UNODC proposes an intervention based on the following outcomes:

Outcome 1 will focus on strengthening national drug control responses by improving national criminal investigation services&#x2019; operational capacities to more effectively counter the growing challenges posed by organized criminal groups and illicit trafficking as well as enhancing referral mechanism for drug users;
Outcome 2 will aim at enhancing ISF judicial police&#x2019;s capacities to address drug-related issues and conduct focused investigations based on reliable forensic services, including through the delivery of a comprehensive equipment and training programme package; 
Outcome 3 at supporting ISF&#x2019;s role in drug prevention interventions, in particular promoting drug awareness in schools and universities, as well as in communities and in detention centres.</narrative>
  </description>
